## Frequently Asked Questions

### Should I sell my 401(k) when the market drops?
Deciding whether to sell depends on your time horizon and goals, though this page cannot judge your individual situation. The [Financial Industry Regulatory Authority (FINRA)](https://www.finra.org/investors/insights/tips-turbulent-market) advises investors to clarify goals tied to a long-term plan, diversify across and within asset classes, and avoid impulsive moves in volatile markets. FINRA also notes that dollar-cost averaging can reduce emotional decision-making during market downturns.

### How much does my 401(k) need to gain to recover from a 20% drop?
Your balance needs a 25.00% gain to recover from a 20% drop. A 20% drop from a hypothetical $100,000 balance leaves $80,000, which takes about 3.3 years to recover at a constant 7% return assuming no ongoing contributions, fees, taxes, or inflation. Because real market returns vary over time, actual recovery timelines will differ.